<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ============================================================================
     MapControlsStrip — the map's tools, ON the map. It is the CONTENT of the vertical MAP-TOOLS RAIL (2026-11-04, the
     user's call — it was the bottom chrome's horizontal tier): MainWindow's MapToolsRail (in the TEMPORAL PANES layer)
     supplies the raised surface, the map-side shade and the 8 px left padding. View → Map tools shows / hides it.

         ┌ top menu bar ─────────────
         ├────┐                         one COLUMN, CENTRED top to bottom in the rail, in the user's order:
         │    │░
         │ ◗▸ │░   0 · RADAR NETWORKS — which networks' site keys show (NEXRAD / TDWR / research; list opens RIGHT)
         │ ⁘  │░       ─ separator
         │ ▤▸ │░   1 · MAP LAYERS — the map key + its car (the layers flyout opens to the RIGHT)
         │ ⁘  │░       ─ separator
         │ ⛶  │░   2 · FIT TO VIEW
         │ ↻  │░   3 · RESET NORTH
         │ ⁘  │░       ─ separator
         │ ◍  │░   4 · MARKERS — the marker viewer, a PLACEHOLDER (no Click yet)
         │ ⊚  │░   5 · LOCATION (lit = your marker is out)
         │    │░
         └────┘     48 wide: 8 padding + a 32 key + the 8 px car on the map key's row

     ⚠️ PANE MODE AND ISOLATION LEFT THIS STRIP (2026-11-04): both are top-menu-bar items now (MainWindow.xaml, TOP MENU
     BAR — Pane Mode menu, Isolation = a SectionedComboBox drawn as a menu title). The SITE PICKER, INSPECT and RINGS/RULER
     live in the floating console's top row (Composites/RadarConsoleHeader); the NETWORK PICKER came back here (2026-11-04),
     on top — it decides which site keys the MAP shows, so it belongs with the map's tools. Place search is centred on
     the top menu bar (Composites/PlaceSearchBox).
     ─ = Primitives/MapControlsStripSeparator, a faint 3 × 3 DOT GRID between GROUPS, centred under the keys (Width 32)
         with generous vertical margins. Tune dot size/gap/brush on the control, not here.

     ⚠️ THERE IS NO LINE ON THE RAIL. Its map side throws a shade onto the map (or, with the EDGE-HATCH bolt-on, the
     hatch). The group SEPARATORS are not seams: they are small dot grids between tools.

     ⚠️ ITS HOVER IS THE RAISED PAIR, and that is not a detail. A control resting on the raised
     surface cannot hover to OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush — in dark the raised ground (#141414) is
     already past it (#1A1A1A), so the hover would be invisible; in light it would go the wrong way.
     Each tier hovers one step further from its OWN ground.

     ⚠️ LOCATION LATCHES: as a plain button it would be a one-way door (nothing else in the shipped UI
     removes the marker — the Selected Marker window is pending re-add). Lit = your marker is out; clicking
     it lit removes it. ⚠️ IsChecked is ONE-WAY and re-asserted after the await in the handler: the locate
     can FAIL without any property changing, so nothing else would pull the toggle back down. Don't make
     it TwoWay. The tooltip carries "Locating…" / "Location unavailable" — a failure is otherwise silent.
     ⚠️ Its mark is a DRAWN reticle (PathIcon, 18-unit box), the same family as the on-map marker — a key
     pictures what it drops. That is why the Inspect key (on the console) is a magnifier; don't give it a reticle.
     ⚠️ The viewer's mark is a drawn TEARDROP, the search pin's shape. Its button has NO Click on purpose;
     wire it when the marker window exists (open bool + WindowManager registration — CLAUDE.md "Add a window").

     MAP LAYERS sits FIRST (Basemap = BasemapViewModel).
     The KEY hides the whole basemap: a blank, THEME-coloured ground (styles/themes/ anvil-map-blank) under the overlays,
     for screenshots / thumbnails / a clean storm. LIT = THE MAP IS SHOWING (default lit); the tooltip speaks
     for the click. The CAR (▸, beside the key on the map side) opens the layer flyout to the RIGHT: which basemap GROUPS
     draw, as a TREE of expanders (Roads by kind, Place names by cities / POIs / water — so you can keep only highways).
     Expanders start closed and aren't persisted; the ticks are. The dimmer is GONE (the user's call, 2026-10-01).
     ⚠️ Hiding OVERRIDES the ticks without changing them — show again and your set returns (the flyout says so
     while hidden). ⚠️ The hide is SESSION-ONLY; the ticks persist.
     ⚠️ A pair of 32 px tools, not a bar key: bar keys are 72 px.

     ⚠️ GREYED WHILE THE PASTCAST LOADING SCREEN IS UP (Radar.AreControlsLocked, 2026-10-04): EVERY tool here, Location
     and the marker viewer included — the map is frosted and gated, so a live tool would only look broken. A new tool
     binds IsEnabled to Free(...) / FreeAnd(...) too.

     Host contract: ViewModel (MapViewModel). Add a tool = one Button in MapToolsColumn, in its group.
     ============================================================================ -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.MapControlsStrip"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:vm="using:Anvil.ViewModels"
             xmlns:models="using:Anvil.Models"
             xmlns:conv="using:Anvil.Converters"
             xmlns:comp="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <!-- A LIT toggle's mark colour (StripToolToggleStyle's Checked states read it). Primary text by default;
                 a toggle may override it in its OWN Resources (the old site toggles did, with their network hue). -->
            <ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Default">
                    <StaticResource x:Key="StripToolCheckedGlyph" ResourceKey="TextFillColorPrimaryBrush"/>
                </ResourceDictionary>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Light">
                    <StaticResource x:Key="StripToolCheckedGlyph" ResourceKey="TextFillColorPrimaryBrush"/>
                </ResourceDictionary>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="HighContrast">
                    <StaticResource x:Key="StripToolCheckedGlyph" ResourceKey="TextFillColorPrimaryBrush"/>
                </ResourceDictionary>
            </ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>

            <!-- ⚠️ EVERY DRAWN MARK GETS ITS FULL 18 × 18 BOX (implicit, so every PathIcon on the tier). A PathIcon is
                 otherwise sized from (0,0) to its geometry's far corner, so a mark drawn in the MIDDLE of the 18-unit
                 design box came out off-centre by however much empty space sat above/left of it — the ruler (drawn
                 y 6–12) sat 3 px low. Fixed to the design box, every mark is centred on (9,9) as drawn. A mark designed
                 in a different box sets its own Width/Height (the map-layers caret). -->
            <Style TargetType="PathIcon">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="18"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="18"/>
            </Style>

            <!-- ⭐ GLYPH SIZE — TUNE HERE (the user's note, 2026-10-10: bigger marks, SAME bar height). The keys stay 32 × 32,
                 so the tier never grows; only the mark inside does. Drawn marks are designed in the 18-unit box above and
                 a PathIcon can't stretch, so each sits in a Viewbox (StripGlyphBox) that scales it to StripGlyphSize. The
                 pane-layout marks are plain Grids sized to it; font glyphs take StripFontGlyphSize (a font's glyph is a
                 bit smaller than its em, hence 20 beside 22). Keep both under the key's 30 inner px. -->
            <x:Double x:Key="StripGlyphSize">22</x:Double>
            <x:Double x:Key="StripFontGlyphSize">20</x:Double>
            <Style x:Key="StripGlyphBox" TargetType="Viewbox">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="{StaticResource StripGlyphSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource StripGlyphSize}"/>
            </Style>

            <!-- A tool button. LOCAL, not in Styles.xaml: this strip is its only consumer, which is that
                 file's house rule. Deliberately NOT the bar-key chain — a bar key is a 72px square carrying
                 a mark over a NAME, and a row of those would make this a second bar rather than a tier of
                 tools. Minimal template so it stays opaque in every state and cannot pick up the stock
                 button's chrome. -->
            <Style x:Key="StripToolButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="5"/>
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="Template">
                    <Setter.Value>
                        <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                            <Grid x:Name="Root"
                                  Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                  BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                  BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                  CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                                <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                    </VisualStateGroup>
                                </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <ContentPresenter x:Name="Glyph"
                                                  HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                  Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                                  Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </ControlTemplate>
                    </Setter.Value>
                </Setter>
            </Style>

            <!-- The LATCHING tool (Location): StripToolButtonStyle's look plus the bar's lit vocabulary — accent
                 BORDER + Elevated face while checked (Elevated is "a control that is ON", never a tier). A separate
                 style because a Button style can't target a ToggleButton. -->
            <!-- ⚠️ OFF IS DIMMER: an unlit toggle's mark is the SECONDARY text colour (it read too bright beside the
                 lit ones); CHECKED — and hovering an unlit one — lifts it to PRIMARY. CHECKED reads the
                 StripToolCheckedGlyph key (top of these resources), so one toggle can light in its own colour. -->
            <Style x:Key="StripToolToggleStyle" TargetType="ToggleButton">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="5"/>
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="Template">
                    <Setter.Value>
                        <ControlTemplate TargetType="ToggleButton">
                            <Grid x:Name="Root"
                                  Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                  BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                  BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                  CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                                <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Checked">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource StripToolCheckedGlyph}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPointerOver">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource StripToolCheckedGlyph}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPressed">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource StripToolCheckedGlyph}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="CheckedDisabled">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                    </VisualStateGroup>
                                </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <ContentPresenter x:Name="Glyph"
                                                  HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                  Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                                  Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </ControlTemplate>
                    </Setter.Value>
                </Setter>
            </Style>


        </ResourceDictionary>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- ⚠️ NO Background here: MainWindow's MapToolsRail paints the raised surface, and a second opaque fill would be one
         more place the rail's colour is written. ONE column, top to bottom in the user's order (the header). Keys are
         Left-aligned at the rail's 8 px padding so the map key's car can sit beside it on the map side. -->
    <StackPanel x:Name="MapToolsColumn" Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="4">
        <!-- ===== 0 · RADAR NETWORKS — which networks' site keys show on the map (Primitives/MapControlsStripNetworkPicker,
             moved here from the console's top row, 2026-11-04). TwoWay + persisted; its list opens to the RIGHT. ===== -->
        <prim:MapControlsStripNetworkPicker x:Name="MapControlsStripNetworkPicker"
                                            IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                                            ShowNexrad="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowNexradSites, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                            ShowTdwr="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowTdwrs, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                            ShowResearch="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowResearchRadars, Mode=TwoWay}"/>

        <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator x:Name="MapToolsSeparatorNetworks" Width="32" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Margin="0,8"/>

        <!-- ===== 1 · MAP LAYERS — the basemap's key + its layer flyout (see the header) =====
             A pair: the KEY hides/shows the whole basemap, the narrow CAR opens the flyout to the right. Plain TwoWay on
             the key (a click always flips it). -->
        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
            <ToggleButton x:Name="MapShownToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind MapShownTooltip(ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown), Mode=OneWay}">
                <!-- A folded map: three panels, the middle one set back. Drawn, not an unverified glyph. -->
                <Viewbox Style="{StaticResource StripGlyphBox}"><PathIcon Data="M1,3.6 L5.4,1.8 L5.4,14.6 L1,16.4 Z M6.6,1.8 L11.4,3.6 L11.4,16.4 L6.6,14.6 Z M12.6,3.6 L17,1.8 L17,14.6 L12.6,16.4 Z"/></Viewbox>
            </ToggleButton>
            <Button x:Name="MapLayersButton"
                    Width="8"
                    IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                    Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                    CornerRadius="3"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Map layers">
                <!-- A right-pointing caret in its own 6 × 10 box (it overrides the implicit 18 × 18). -->
                <PathIcon Data="M1,1 L5,5 L1,9 Z" Width="6" Height="10"/>
                <Button.Flyout>
                    <!-- ⚠️ Windowed (ShouldConstrainToRootBounds=False), like every flyout over the map — else the owned
                         panel windows paint over it. Opens to the RIGHT of the rail, onto the map. -->
                    <Flyout Placement="RightEdgeAlignedTop" ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False">
                        <StackPanel Width="220" Spacing="2">
                            <TextBlock Text="Map layers" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="The map is hidden. These apply when you show it."
                                       TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12" Margin="0,0,0,4"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"
                                       Visibility="{x:Bind HiddenNoteVisibility(ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                            <!-- THE TREE: one row per category (BasemapCategory). Every row reserves a 20 px
                                 chevron column, so plain rows' boxes line up with the expanders'. An expander's
                                 box is a ONE-WAY select-all (Click → ToggleAll; ■ = partial), DragMoveLayerExpander's
                                 rule; its leaves indent 48 (the parent's box column 24 + one more step) and bind TWO-WAY. Wrappers carry
                                 the tooltips: a disabled CheckBox shows none. -->
                            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Basemap.Categories}">
                                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:BasemapCategory">
                                        <StackPanel>
                                            <Grid ColumnSpacing="4" Background="Transparent"
                                                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ToolTip, Mode=OneWay}">
                                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="20"/>
                                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                                <Button Width="20" Height="20" MinWidth="0" MinHeight="0" Padding="0"
                                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                        Background="Transparent" BorderThickness="0" CornerRadius="4"
                                                        Visibility="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.VisibleIf(HasChildren)}"
                                                        AutomationProperties.Name="{x:Bind Label}"
                                                        Click="{x:Bind ToggleExpanded}">
                                                    <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE76C;" FontSize="10"
                                                              Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                                                              RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
                                                        <FontIcon.RenderTransform>
                                                            <RotateTransform Angle="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.ChevronAngle(IsExpanded), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                                        </FontIcon.RenderTransform>
                                                    </FontIcon>
                                                </Button>
                                                <CheckBox Grid.Column="1" Content="{x:Bind Label}" MinHeight="32"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind IsChecked, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind IsAvailable, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="{x:Bind ToggleAll}"/>
                                            </Grid>
                                            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind Leaves}" Margin="48,0,0,0"
                                                          Visibility="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.VisibleIf(IsExpanded), Mode=OneWay}">
                                                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:BasemapGroupOption">
                                                        <Grid Background="Transparent"
                                                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ToolTip, Mode=OneWay}">
                                                            <CheckBox Content="{x:Bind Label}" MinHeight="32"
                                                                      IsChecked="{x:Bind IsShown, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                                      IsEnabled="{x:Bind IsAvailable, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                                        </Grid>
                                                    </DataTemplate>
                                                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                            </ItemsControl>
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </DataTemplate>
                                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                            </ItemsControl>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Flyout>
                </Button.Flyout>
            </Button>
        </StackPanel>

        <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator x:Name="MapToolsSeparatorLayers" Width="32" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Margin="0,8"/>

        <!-- ===== 2 · FIT TO VIEW — frame the effective region (isolated state, else CONUS). ===== -->
        <Button x:Name="FitToViewButton"
                Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                Click="OnFitToViewClick"
                IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Fit To View">
            <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="{StaticResource StripFontGlyphSize}" Glyph="&#xE740;"/>
        </Button>

        <!-- ===== 3 · RESET NORTH — undo a right-drag rotate/tilt. ===== -->
        <Button x:Name="ResetNorthButton"
                Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                Click="OnResetNorthClick"
                IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Reset North/Flat">
            <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="{StaticResource StripFontGlyphSize}" Glyph="&#xE72C;"/>
        </Button>

        <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator x:Name="MapToolsSeparatorWhere" Width="32" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Margin="0,8"/>

        <!-- ===== 4 · MARKERS — the marker viewer, a PLACEHOLDER. No Click until the marker window exists (see the header).
             A teardrop with an eye, the search pin's own shape. ===== -->
        <Button x:Name="MarkerViewerButton"
                Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Markers (coming soon)">
            <Viewbox Style="{StaticResource StripGlyphBox}"><PathIcon Data="M9,0 C5.1,0 2,3.1 2,7 C2,12 9,18 9,18 C9,18 16,12 16,7 C16,3.1 12.9,0 9,0 Z M9,4.5 A2.5,2.5 0 1,0 9,9.5 A2.5,2.5 0 1,0 9,4.5 Z"/></Viewbox>
        </Button>

        <!-- ===== 5 · LOCATION — drop / remove your marker. ONE-WAY IsChecked, re-asserted in the handler. ===== -->
        <ToggleButton x:Name="LocationToggle"
                      Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                      IsEnabled="{x:Bind FreeAnd(ViewModel.Markers.CanLocate, ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                      IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Markers.HasUserLocationMarker, Mode=OneWay}"
                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind LocationTooltip(ViewModel.Markers.HasUserLocationMarker, ViewModel.Markers.LocateStatusText), Mode=OneWay}"
                      Click="OnToggleUserLocation">
            <!-- Ring (donut 3.6-5.2), SOLID core (r 2.2), four ticks standing off it. -->
            <Viewbox Style="{StaticResource StripGlyphBox}"><PathIcon Data="M3.8,9 A5.2,5.2 0 1,0 14.2,9 A5.2,5.2 0 1,0 3.8,9 Z M5.4,9 A3.6,3.6 0 1,0 12.6,9 A3.6,3.6 0 1,0 5.4,9 Z M6.8,9 A2.2,2.2 0 1,0 11.2,9 A2.2,2.2 0 1,0 6.8,9 Z M8.2,0 H9.8 V3 H8.2 Z M8.2,15 H9.8 V18 H8.2 Z M0,8.2 H3 V9.8 H0 Z M15,8.2 H18 V9.8 H15 Z"/></Viewbox>
        </ToggleButton>
    </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
